  "name": "create-server-runnable-with-operation-events",
  "description": "A server runnable, started by client calls of two operations through the component's own provide port and declared `concurrent`, authored with no new tool and no new addressing: the port and the runnable are `create`s, and each operation event is a `create` at its own `whole_value` member address, `{member: {type: operation, port, operation}}` (contract `7.7.0`). The delta folds the two event creates into the runnable's, because the runnable is new — one reviewed unit per element the change set adds.",
  "kind": "example",
  "context": {
    "summary": "The `examples/basic` model. `IDiagnosticService` is the client-server interface declaring `ReadDtc` and `ClearDtc`, whose two signatures are the same (`uint16` in, `uint8` out), so one runnable may serve both: `check-model`'s partial `[constr_2000]` finds nothing to report. `ExampleSWC` provides no port on it yet. No component declares an ASIL, and the safety rules read no event and no `concurrent`, so the change set asks no safety question.",
    "existing_elements": [
      {
        "layer": "swc",
        "element": "ExampleSWC"
      },
