    "notes": "An operation event has no identity field, so it is addressed by its whole value, like a timing event — `(type, port, operation)` is what makes it one event, and two events naming one pair are one `duplicate-binding` finding, never an identity conflict. `concurrent` is the runnable's own field (AUTOSAR's `canBeInvokedConcurrently`), written only when `true`, so the file this commits carries `concurrent: true` between the runnable's name and its events. The runnable is started by operation events alone; one that also carried a timing event would be accepted as written, because SWCraft does not judge mixed event kinds."
